wn and Glade Mills are near the center of the township along Pennsylvania Route 8, which crosses the township from north to south. According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of , of which is land and , or 0.31%, is water. Deer Creek and Bull Creek originate in the southeast section\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d01\", \"text\": \"south to the Allegheny River in Allegheny County. [ 4 ] Demographics [ edit ] Historical population Census Pop. Note % ± 2010 12,345 — 2020 15,671 27.0% 2022 ( est. ) 16,895 [ 2 ] 7.8% U.S. Decennial Census [ 5 ] As of the 2000 census, [ 6 ] there were 12,345 people, 2,045 households, and 1,615 families residing in the township. The population density was 543.2 inhabitants per square mile ( 210.0/km 2 ). There were 2,105 housing units at an average density of 91.7 per square mile ( 35.4/km 2 ).\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d02\", \"text\": \"Middlesex Township, Butler County, Pennsylvania Middlesex Township is a township in Butler County, Pennsylvania, United States. The population was 12,450 at the 2010 census. Middlesex Township is located in south-central Butler County, with Allegheny County to the south. The unincorporated communities of Cooperstown and Glade Mills are near the center of the township along Pennsylvania Route 8, which crosses the township from north to south. According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of, of which is land and, or 0.31%, is water. Deer Creek and Bull Creek originate in the southeast section.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d03\", \"text\": \", of which is land and , or 1.05%, is water. As of the census of 2000, there were 6,669 people, 2,298 households, and 1,730 families residing in the township. The population density was 257.2 people per square mile (99.3/km²). There were 2,392 housing units at an average density of 92.3/sq mi (35.6/km²). The racial makeup of the township was 95.98% White, 1.50% African American, 0.10% Native American, 0.79% Asian, 0.04% Pacific Islander, 0.43% from other races, and 1.14% from two or more races. 1.26% of the population were Hispanic or Latino of any race. There were 2,298 households, out\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d04\", \"text\": \"6,669 people , 2,298 households , and 1,730 families residing in the township . The population density was 257.2 inhabitants per square mile ( 99.3/km 2 ) . There were 2,392 housing units at an average density of 92.3 units per square mile ( 35.6 units/km 2 ) . The racial makeup of the township was 95.98 % White , 1.50 % African American , 0.10 % Native American , 0.79 % Asian , 0.04 % Pacific Islander , 0.43 % from other races , and 1.14 % from two or more races . 1.26 % of the population were\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"I do not have specific information on the population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania\", \"scope\": \"2010 census\", \"claim\": \"The population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania was 5,390 at the 2010 census.\", \"answer\": \"5,390\", \"quote\": \"The population was 5,390 at the 2010 census.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania\", \"scope\": \"as of 2022 (est.)\", \"claim\": \"The population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania is 16,895 as of 2022 (est.).\", \"answer\": \"16,895\", \"quote\": \"Note % ± 2010 12,345 — 2020 15,671 27.0% 2022 ( est. ) 16,895 [ 2 ] 7.8% U.S.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0218-83d4364cd84b:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"population of Middlesex Township, Pennsylvania\", \"scope\": \"2010 cens